Atlas reads ExLlamaV3's EXL3 format (its trellis layout and bitstream, its
"3inst", "mcg" and "mul1" codebooks, its half-integer bit widths, its
tensor-core fragment order and its Hadamard-rotated scales). Atlas translates
TensorFold's Zig reader and reference decoder of that format into Rust, and
copies and adapts TensorFold's EXL3 CUDA kernels; TensorFold's implementations
are its own, checked by TensorFold bit for bit against ExLlamaV3's
dequantization, and no ExLlamaV3 source is copied. The files that carry it are
listed, with the upstream paths and line ranges and the changes made, in
EXL3-ATTRIBUTION.md:
